his tenure as coach of Germany's national men's football team. Can his charisma alone push this group forward?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6036ae8ad440f3b6d97e2c470a78ad15f732a29105388f440065f5aa8a9bdc0e</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Franz Reindl elected new IIHF president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19c194e0d963f0cfb5169e2635bb3a07c86652884a9ab6b52197a433b9dae9cf</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799--24f017ae08ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-franz-reindl-elected-new-iihf-president/a-79521799?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Franz Reindl has been elected president of ice hockey's world governing body. The former forward was a member of West Germany's Olympic bronze medal-winning team.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d6bf5e646705c970bc9db9df0dcfff8ef078741cc4d6d2c3149b6939fd2bcd8</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Cristiano Ronaldo walks out of Portugal camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50b353d60409190891972072ce327c7afe4c6c8130bf807860f2d1794253996b</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238--be4e02847569.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cristiano Ronaldo has left Portugal’s camp after learning that he would not start the next Nations League match. Portugal's coach has denied reports of a rift between himself and the star player.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e85945a01edbb5bf6f48b065d15d2b7a20b77bbf2f371c2f3e4f80db76d5abba</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What do Manchester City's charges mean for German football?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:134a7caf8f938ebbcd3c5017f36000956c2aa4f7e2517eb7bb53f3934a37ad15</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412--ba8ebfa60874.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-do-manchester-city-s-charges-mean-for-german-football/a-79460412?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manchester City have reportedly been found guilty of major financial rule breaches. What does this mean for German football?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland beat Israel 3-0 in Nations League match overshadowed by political controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:985c887a04f74db83de2f033b9678e5ce9eec185e2c318768d604221606c8ed8</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T09:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254--ac737f0c12b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-beat-israel-3-0-in-nations-league-match-overshadowed-by-political-controversy/a-79455254?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ireland easily beat Israel in a Nations League fixture that 24 hours earlier appeared in doubt. One Irish player pulled out of the match to express his opposition to Israel's actions in the Gaza Strip.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2202928b8e2b1643db54555bc09c31b9e218f826467d01bd20df918d7a65e88</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e90b6d59a2e3c675848910ff0c873dfdda580ca17391be813bbe36a0d601bb91</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74df50533b287be4dad607760acae0df2802108062a69ba0e7135025ef17eb01</id><updated>2026-10-03T13:32:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
